  },
  "description": "EKOBIP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C32 H65 N14 Nd5 O27,C2 H6 O1. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd1E (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd2E (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3E (Nd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.660-5.508 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.28-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C32H65N14O27Nd5·(CH3CH2OH). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ5-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
